                "old_text": "# Helpers\n\nUtilities.\n",
                "new_text": "# Helpers\n\nUtility functions for small examples.\n\n## numbers.total\n\nSum numeric values in an iterable, ignoring `None` elements.\n\n- `None` values are skipped.\n- Zero and negative numbers are included.\n- An empty iterable or one containing only `None` returns `0`.\n\nExamples:\n\n```python\nfrom numbers import total\n\ntotal([2, None, -1, 0])  # 1\ntotal([None])            # 0\ntotal([])                # 0\n```\n\n## labels.normalize\n\nNormalize text by stripping leading/trailing whitespace and lowercasing.\n\n- Leading and trailing whitespace characters are removed.\n- Internal spaces are preserved.\n- Empty or all-whitespace input becomes an empty string.\n\nExamples:\n\n```python\nfrom labels import normalize\n\nnormalize(\" A B \")   # \"a b\"\nnormalize(\"  \")      # \"\"\nnormalize(\"Hello\")   # \"hello\"\n```\n"
              }
            ]
